      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-146522",
      ":question/problem": "$f(x, y) = {\\frac{3}{11}(x + y^{2}),\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 1, 0 \\le y \\le 2 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nThe joint probability density function $f(x, y)$ for the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that\n$E[X] = \\frac{6}{11}, E[Y] = \\frac{15}{11}, SD[X] \\approx 0.2851, SD[Y] \\approx 0.4996$,\nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y$. Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
